<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<?xml-stylesheet href="xsd.xsl" type="text/xsl"?>
<!--* Substitute this schema document for ACSJournal-namespace.xsd,
    * in order to use substitution groups to extend MathML.
    *-->
<!--* Changes:
    * Add xmlns:m and xmlns:xlink namespace declarations 
    * Add xsl:import for MathML namespaces
    * Add substitutionGroup="m:mspace" to ACS element declarations
    * Add types to serve as bridges to m:mspace
    *-->
<xsd:schema xmlns:ACS="http://namespace.acs.org/2008/acs"
            xmlns:mtl="http://www.mulberrytech.com/taglib"
            xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema"
            xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"            
            xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
            targetNamespace="http://namespace.acs.org/2008/acs">
   <xsd:annotation>
      <xsd:documentation>
         <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" class="bodytext">
            <h1>MODULE: ACS_XSD_schema_document</h1>
            <h2>VERSION:  0.1</h2>
            <h2>DATE:  Wed_May_11_21:58:33_EDT_2022</h2>
            <dl>
               <dt>SYSTEM</dt>
               <dd>
                  <p>ACS_DTD_in_XSD</p>
               </dd>
               <dt>PURPOSE</dt>
               <dd>
                  <p>Declare_elements_in_ACS_namespace</p>
               </dd>
               <dt>CREATED FOR</dt>
               <dd>
                  <p>American_Chemical_Society</p>
                  <p>Original Creation Date December_2013</p>
               </dd>
               <dt>CREATED BY</dt>
               <dd>Mulberry Technologies, Inc.                       
             <br/>17 West Jefferson Street, #207                    
             <br/>Rockville, MD 20850 (301-315-9631)                
             <br/>http://www.mulberrytech.com                       
             <br/>(B._T._Usdin_and_C._M._Sperberg-McQueen)</dd>
            </dl>
         </div>
      </xsd:documentation>
   </xsd:annotation>

   <xsd:import namespace="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"/>
   <xsd:import namespace="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"/>


   <xsd:annotation>
      <xsd:documentation>
         <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" class="bodytext">
	   <p>First, we declare the ACS extension elements.
	   We use named types, not inline types, so as to
	   keep all the type-related machinery separate from
	   the element declarations.</p>
	   <p>Each element goes into the substitution group
	   of element <code>m:space</code> in the MathML namespace.
	   That means they can appear wherever <code>m:space</code>
	   is mentioned in a content model.</p>
         </div>
      </xsd:documentation>
   </xsd:annotation>
 
   <xsd:element name="marker" 
		type="ACS:marker.type" 
		substitutionGroup="m:mspace"/>
   
   <xsd:element name="tie-bar-end" 
		type="ACS:tie-bar-end.type" 
		substitutionGroup="m:mspace"/>
   
   <xsd:element name="tie-bar-start" 
		type="ACS:tie-bar-start.type" 
		substitutionGroup="m:mspace"/>

      <xsd:annotation>
         <xsd:documentation>
         <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" class="bodytext">
	   <p>Next, we declare the three types.  In order to make
	   the elements with these types substitutable for 
	   <code>m:space</code>, the types must be derived from
	   <code>m:space.type</code> (as the name suggests, this is
	   the type of element <code>m:space</code>) by a series
	   of extension or restriction steps.  We'll do this
	   in several steps, building a bridge from 
	   <code>m:space.type</code> to the types needed for
	   the ACS extension elements.</p>
	 </div>
      </xsd:documentation>
     </xsd:annotation>

   <xsd:complexType name="bridge-with-id">
     <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>
	 <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" class="bodytext">	 
	   <p>First step: a bridge type which retains the ID
	   attribute from <code>m:space</code>, and deletes
	   all the other attributes.</p>
	   <p>This type has no content, and just the one attribute ID.</p>
         </div>
       </xsd:documentation>
     </xsd:annotation>
     <xsd:complexContent>
       <xsd:restriction base="m:mspace.type">
         <xsd:attribute name="width" use="prohibited"/>
         <xsd:attribute name="height" use="prohibited"/>
         <xsd:attribute name="depth" use="prohibited"/>
         <xsd:attribute name="linebreak" use="prohibited"/>
         <xsd:attribute name="class" use="prohibited"/>
         <xsd:attribute name="style" use="prohibited"/>
         <xsd:attribute name="xref" use="prohibited"/>
         <xsd:attribute ref="xlink:href" use="prohibited"/>
       </xsd:restriction>
     </xsd:complexContent>
   </xsd:complexType>
  
  <xsd:complexType name="bridge-no-id">
     <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>
	 <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" class="bodytext">	 
	   <p>Next step: a bridge type which drops the ID
	   attribute from <code>m:space</code>, too.</p>
	   <p>This type has no content and no attributes; it's
	   pretty much a blank slate.</p>
            </div>
         </xsd:documentation>
      </xsd:annotation>
     <xsd:complexContent>
       <xsd:restriction base="ACS:bridge-with-id">
         <xsd:attribute name="id" use="prohibited"/>
       </xsd:restriction>
     </xsd:complexContent>
   </xsd:complexType>
  
  <xsd:complexType name="bridge-required-id">
     <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>
	 <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" class="bodytext">	 
	   <p>Next step: a bridge type which <em>requires</em> the ID
	   attribute.  This is a restriction of type
	   <code>ACS:bridge-with-id</code>.  It's not particularly
	   useful in itself but it forms the basis for
	   <code>ACS:tie-bar-start.type</code>.</p>
         </div>
       </xsd:documentation>
     </xsd:annotation>
    <xsd:complexContent>
      <xsd:restriction base="ACS:bridge-with-id">
        <xsd:attribute name="id" type="xsd:ID" use="required"/>
      </xsd:restriction>
    </xsd:complexContent>
  </xsd:complexType>
  
  <xsd:complexType name="marker.type">
     <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>
	 <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" class="bodytext">	 
	   <p>This type (<code>ACS:marker.type</code> inherits an
	   optional ID attribute from <code>m:space.type</code>
	   (through <code>ACS:bridge-with-id</code>), and adds
	   two further attributes.</p>
         </div>
       </xsd:documentation>
     </xsd:annotation>
    <xsd:complexContent mixed="true">
      <xsd:extension base="ACS:bridge-with-id">        
         <xsd:attribute name="marker-type" use="required" type="xsd:NMTOKEN"/>
         <xsd:attribute name="rid" use="optional" type="xsd:IDREFS"/>
      </xsd:extension>
    </xsd:complexContent>
      </xsd:complexType>
  
  <xsd:complexType name="tie-bar-end.type">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>
	 <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" class="bodytext">	 
	   <p>This type (<code>ACS:tie-bar-end.type</code> carries
	   only an <code>rid</code> attribute.</p>
	   <p>It has no particular similarity to <code>m:space.type</code>,
	   and we wouldn't derive it from that type except that we
	   must, in order to be in the substitution group of element
	   <code>m:space</code>.</p>
         </div>
       </xsd:documentation>
      </xsd:annotation>
    <xsd:complexContent>
      <xsd:extension base="ACS:bridge-no-id">
         <xsd:attribute name="rid" use="required" type="xsd:IDREF"/>
      </xsd:extension>
    </xsd:complexContent>
      </xsd:complexType>
  
  <xsd:complexType name="tie-bar-start.type">
      <xsd:annotation>
       <xsd:documentation>
	 <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" class="bodytext">	 
	   <p>This type (<code>ACS:tie-bar-start.type</code> inherits
	   the required ID attribute from <code>ACS:bridge-required-id</code>
	   and adds a <code>position</code> attribute.</p>
         </div>
       </xsd:documentation>
      </xsd:annotation>
    <xsd:complexContent mixed="true">
      <xsd:extension base="ACS:bridge-required-id">
         <xsd:attribute name="position" use="required">
                     <xsd:simpleType>
                        <xsd:annotation>
                  <xsd:documentation/>
               </xsd:annotation>
                        <xsd:restriction base="xsd:NMTOKEN">
                           <xsd:enumeration value="above"/>
                           <xsd:enumeration value="below"/>
                        </xsd:restriction>
                     </xsd:simpleType>
                  </xsd:attribute>
      </xsd:extension>
    </xsd:complexContent>
      </xsd:complexType>
</xsd:schema>

